WEBVTT

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:34.228
Because the plankton that are here today
clean that carbon out of the air.

00:02:34.252 --> 00:02:36.483
But you see, they don't really
hold a grudge.

00:02:36.507 --> 00:02:38.085
(Laughter)

00:02:38.109 --> 00:02:40.578
The problem is they cannot keep up

00:02:40.602 --> 00:02:44.302
with the tremendous amount
of carbon we are dumping into the air.

00:02:45.093 --> 00:02:46.760
So what does all of this mean?

00:02:46.784 --> 00:02:49.148
Well, it means
that our big carbon footprint

00:02:49.172 --> 00:02:52.446
is crushing the very creatures
that sustain us.

00:02:52.784 --> 00:02:54.149
And yes, like Tom said,

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:57.164
killing almost half of the creatures
that allow us to breathe

00:02:57.188 --> 00:02:58.655
is a really big deal.

00:02:59.307 --> 00:03:01.291
So you're probably asking yourself: